<!-- Forge's screens over the game (port/linux/game/forge.c), built into each level's map with the
pause screen (ingame.txt; its fonts and pictures are halo3/pause.xml's, the same set):
- the object browser (Square, as the monitor: forge.c opens it), Halo Online's and the mockup's
  window at the right over the running game, which it does not pause, as Halo 3's does not: the
  title strip with the budget, the crumb (OBJECTS > VEHICLES), the list with the orange bar and the
  count placed, the pane on the one chosen, the button strip. The categories first, A opens one, L
  and R step through them, A on an object places it in the monitor's hand, B goes back, Square
  closes it;
- the Forge menu, Start in a Forge game (menu_tags.c opens it for the level's pause screen): resume,
  the monitor or the Spartan, save the map variant (its name typed on the system's keyboard: port
  forge save), undo and redo (forge.c's history), snapping on or off, every placed character's AI
  on or off, the dead characters cleared out of the layout (they hold their places in the AI
  budget until then), every character cleared (asked first), a new round (Halo 3's Restart Round: the map reset, the layout placed again), leave
  (asked first), the controls at the right; what the last of them came to said under the menu;
- the object's properties (Square while holding an object you placed): its team, respawn time and
  whether it is placed at the start, and a character's AI team and AI on or off (those two rows
  hidden for any other object), A or left and right to change one, B to close; kept in the map
  variant;
- the question before leaving.
The art is this folder's own (tools/halo3_menu_art.py). -->
